  "reference_solution": "WITH p AS (SELECT order_id, SUM(COALESCE(amount,0)) AS paid_total FROM payments GROUP BY order_id), i AS (SELECT order_id, SUM(COALESCE(units,0)) AS unit_total FROM items GROUP BY order_id) SELECT o.order_id, COALESCE(p.paid_total,0) AS paid_total, COALESCE(i.unit_total,0) AS unit_total FROM orders o LEFT JOIN p USING(order_id) LEFT JOIN i USING(order_id) WHERE o.status='completed'",
  "solution_explanation": "Aggregate each child to order grain before joining. A direct payment-to-item join multiplies both measures. Drive the result from completed orders and normalize missing aggregates to zero.",
  "hints": [
    "State the output grain before considering joins.",
    "Count how many joined rows one payment can become.",
    "Reduce each child independently to the parent key before enrichment."
  ],
  "senior_review": "A strong review states one row per completed order, validates child uniqueness and reconciles measures before and after enrichment. Result correctness alone does not evaluate that explanation.",
